{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"GeneDx's quarterly volume series shows sequential stalling: Q1'26 fell 1% q/q before Q2 recovered.","detail":"Quarterly volumes: Q1'25 20,562; Q2'25 23,246; Q3'25 ~25,702 (derived); Q4'25 27,761; Q1'26 27,488 (-1.0% q/q); Q2'26 30,785 (+12.0% q/q). Y/y growth went +34.3% (Q4'25), +34% (Q1'26), +32% (Q2'26). The Q1 dip came while the company says it added sequencing capacity, so capacity was not the limit.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001818331/000181833126000039/wgsq12026earningspresent.htm","date":"2026-05-04","source_name":"GeneDx Q1'26 investor presentation","source_type":"filing","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The 2025-26 quarterly series was untabulated. The known list has only Q2'26 (30,785, +32%)."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"GeneDx's genome mix is falling, which lowers sequencing Gb per test just as it adds fleet capacity.","detail":"Genomes were 45% of the exome/genome portfolio in Q1'26. In the insurance outpatient channel they were 32% in Q2, down from close to 40% in Q1 (15% in 2025). Management expects about 30% or slightly less in H2, and reflex volumes exceeded genomes in July 2026 for the first time. Illustratively, Q1 had ~12,370 genomes at ~100 Gb (~1.24 Pb) and ~15,120 exomes at ~10 Gb (~0.15 Pb). Genomes are ~89% of Gb, so a few points of mix move Gb faster than test counts.","url":"https://www.webull.com/news/15381684706632704","date":"2026-08-03","source_name":"GeneDx Q2'26 call transcript (Webull)","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"reflex volumes exceeding genomes in the month of July","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list covers Gb per test by test type but not GeneDx's genome-mix reversal, which is a Gb-per-test drag at a large Illumina customer."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"At GeneDx, payer collection and coverage, not sequencing cost, limit genome growth.","detail":"Outpatient genome collection rate is ~32%, flat versus Q1 and down from 43% a year earlier. Management's mature-test goal is ~70%. It expects Q3 collection flat, with improvement in Q4 and the larger uplift in 2027. Genome cost is nearly 2x exome, mostly reagents, yet management does not call cost the constraint. This fits the thesis that volume is gated outside sequencing.","url":"https://www.webull.com/news/15381684706632704","date":"2026-08-03","source_name":"GeneDx Q2'26 call transcript (Webull)","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list has BillionToOne and Tegus expert versions of the constraint. This is a named large customer with a measured collection rate."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"A large Illumina customer is planning on lower reagent prices: genome reagent cost is ~2x exome, expected to fall as manufacturers advance technology.","detail":"On the Q2'26 call the CFO said whole-genome production cost is nearly double exome, \"almost entirely\" reagents. He expects it to fall with utilization and manufacturer technology advances. Cost per test is said to stay \"relatively flat for the second half of 2026\" with step improvements in 2027. The 2027 timing matches the roadmap 35B flow cell (H1 2027). The customer is therefore budgeting a reagent price cut, which is the leverage the thesis describes.","url":"https://www.webull.com/news/15381684706632704","date":"2026-08-03","source_name":"GeneDx Q2'26 call transcript (Webull)","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"The difference there is almost entirely higher reagent costs.","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list has GeneDx cost/test of about -14% (directional) but not the 2027 step-improvement guide or the reagent attribution."},
