{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"GeneDx's revenue per exome/genome test fell about 12% y/y in Q2'26, so its own price per test is falling, which keeps pressure on its sequencing cost.","detail":"Revenue per test was $3,258 in Q2'26 ($100.3M / 30,785) versus about $3,699 in Q2'25 ($86.0M / 23,246), or -11.9%. Q1 was about $3,296 versus $3,473 (-5%). Q3 guidance is ~$3,343 ($111M / 33,200). The company says contracted pricing is unchanged and the cause is genome mix, so it has less room to absorb a flat reagent price. It reported adjusted gross margin of 70.4% versus 70.6% a year earlier.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001818331/000162828026051852/exhibit991-q22026pressrele.htm","date":"2026-08-03","source_name":"GeneDx Q2'26 8-K Ex. 99.1","source_type":"filing","quote":"There have been no meaningful changes to our contracted pricing.","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known list has GeneDx revenue growing slower than volume. The quantified per-test series and Q3 guide arithmetic are new."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"GeneDx's FY26 guidance cut was driven by reimbursement mix, not volume, but its volume guide was also lowered from 33-35% to at least 30%.","detail":"FY26 revenue guidance was cut from $540-555M (23 Feb) to $475-490M (4 May), a ~$65M or ~12% cut at the midpoint. Exome/genome volume growth went from 33-35% (128-131K tests) to at least 30%. Of the Q1 revenue shortfall, ~$5.5M was lower blended ARR and ~$6.5M was weakness in Fabric and biopharma. The CFO said the initial guide \"proved to be too aggressive\".","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001818331/000181833126000039/wgsq12026earningspresent.htm","date":"2026-05-04","source_name":"GeneDx Q1'26 deck and release (call summary via search snippets)","source_type":"earnings_call","quote":"proved to be too aggressive","strength":"medium","why_new":"The known list has only Q3 volume. The guide-cut sizing, its causes and the prior volume range are new."},
